Relevant columns for the requested statistics  
(starting from the only table we are allowed to use:  
`bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`)

• `reference_name`: filter to chromosome “chr1”.  
• `start_position`: region lower boundary (≥ 55039447).  
• `end_position`: region upper boundary (≤ 55064852 could be used as well, but the
  start position is sufficient for point‐wise variants).  
• `alternate_bases`: ARRAY of STRUCTs that contains, for every alternate allele,  
  – `alt`: the alternate base sequence;  
  – `AC`: allele count in gnomAD (needed for “total allele count”);  
  – `vep`: ARRAY of STRUCTs; inside every element  
   • `SYMBOL`: gene symbol annotation (needed for “distinct gene symbols”).  
• `AN`: number of alleles assessed for the variant site (used for “total number of alleles”).

Filtering condition that will be re‑used in all queries  
```
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
```

------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory–to–final SQL queries
------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Preview raw rows in the interval (first 20)
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show only coordinates and reference / alternate strings
SELECT start_position, end_position, reference_bases, alt.alt AS alt_base
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count how many variants (rows) fall in the region
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n_variants
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect allele count (AC) values for each alternate allele
SELECT start_position, alt.alt AS alt_base, alt.AC
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Aggregate total AC over the region
SELECT SUM(alt.AC) AS total_AC
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 6. Aggregate total AN (alleles observed) over the region
SELECT SUM(AN) AS total_AN
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 7. List distinct gene symbols annotated by VEP
SELECT DISTINCT vep.SYMBOL
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt,
     UNNEST(alt.vep)        AS vep
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND vep.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. How many unique gene symbols are present in the interval?
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT vep.SYMBOL) AS n_genes
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS alt,
     UNNEST(alt.vep)        AS vep
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND vep.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring everything together except density
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT t.start_position)                           AS n_variants,
  SUM(alt.AC)                                                AS total_AC,
  SUM(t.AN)                                                  AS total_AN,
  ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT vep.SYMBOL ORDER BY vep.SYMBOL LIMIT 50) AS gene_symbols
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1` AS t
JOIN UNNEST(t.alternate_bases) AS alt
JOIN UNNEST(alt.vep)          AS vep
WHERE t.reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND t.start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND vep.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final summary including mutation density
--     Region length = 55064852 - 55039447 = 25405 bp
SELECT
  n_variants,
  total_AC,
  total_AN,
  gene_symbols,
  25405.0 / n_variants AS mutation_density_bp_per_variant
FROM (
  SELECT
    COUNT(DISTINCT t.start_position)                           AS n_variants,
    SUM(alt.AC)                                                AS total_AC,
    SUM(t.AN)                                                  AS total_AN,
    ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT vep.SYMBOL ORDER BY vep.SYMBOL)         AS gene_symbols
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1` AS t
  JOIN UNNEST(t.alternate_bases) AS alt
  JOIN UNNEST(alt.vep)          AS vep
  WHERE t.reference_name = 'chr1'
    AND t.start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
    AND vep.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
);
```

Each query is limited to 20 rows where that makes sense (preview‑style queries).  
